**exactly one real solution with every variable in its interval** (`catalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron_nu_system_<j>_oneRoot`:
`PolynomialSystem.HasUniqueRoot`, `Modules/System/PolyRootOf.lean`), and `ν Catalan.DisdyakisTriacontahedron.polyhedron` is the largest scale among
those roots (`catalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron_nu_roots_list`). `catalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron_nu_roots` is the statement in Mathlib's terms alone
(`IsPolyRootMax`, `Modules/System/PolyRoot.lean`), which implies that of the headline `catalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron_nu`
(`IsPolyRootMax.isPolynomialSystemMax`). The system has one variable, the scale, so its one scale (`catalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron_exact_list`) is its one root (`PolynomialSystem.IsMaxSingle.isRootMax_of_one_var`).
Generated by `lean/scripts/exact_n.py` from the theorems of `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandCatalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron` and `Nieuwland.Certs.NieuwlandCatalanDisdyakisTriacontahedron.Exact`,
which it does not change.
-/

